{"id":"mahabharata-7-137","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":137,"title":"सप्तत्रिंशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 137 · Night: Satyaki and Somadatta","summary":{"en":"Satyaki, seeing Somadatta raise his great bow, attacks him, and Bahlika's banner is cut down. Yudhishthira, seeing Satyaki covered with arrows, enters the fight, and Drona seizes Bhima's heel.","kn":"ಸೋಮದತ್ತ ದೊಡ್ಡ ಬಿಲ್ಲು ಎತ್ತುವುದನ್ನು ಕಂಡ ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿ ಅವನ ಮೇಲೆ ಎರಗುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಬಾಹ್ಲೀಕನ ಧ್ವಜ ಕತ್ತರಿಸಲ್ಪಡುತ್ತದೆ. ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿ ಬಾಣಗಳಿಂದ ಮುಚ್ಚಿದುದನ್ನು ಕಂಡ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಹೋರಾಟಕ್ಕೆ ಇಳಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"सोमदत्त को विशाल धनुष उठाते देख सात्यकि उस पर आक्रमण करता है, और बाह्लीक का ध्वज कट जाता है। सात्यकि को बाणों से ढका देख युधिष्ठिर युद्ध में उतरते हैं।","te":"సోమదత్తుడు పెద్ద విల్లు ఎత్తడం చూసి సాత్యకి అతనిపై దాడి చేస్తాడు; బాహ్లీకుని ధ్వజం ఛేదించబడుతుంది. సాత్యకి బాణాలతో కప్పబడటం చూసి యుధిష్ఠిరుడు పోరులోకి దిగుతాడు.","ta":"சோமதத்தன் பெரும் வில்லை உயர்த்துவதைக் கண்ட சாத்யகி அவனைத் தாக்க, பாஹ்லீகனின் கொடி வெட்டப்படுகிறது. அம்புகளால் மூடப்பட்ட சாத்யகியைக் கண்ட யுதிஷ்டிரர் போரில் இறங்குகிறார்.","ml":"സോമദത്തൻ വലിയ വില്ല് ഉയർത്തുന്നത് കണ്ട സാത്യകി അദ്ദേഹത്തെ ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു; ബാഹ്ലികന്റെ കൊടി വെട്ടിവീഴ്ത്തപ്പെടുന്നു. അമ്പുകളാൽ മൂടപ്പെട്ട സാത്യകിയെ കണ്ട് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ പോരാട്ടത്തിൽ ചേരുന്നു; ദ്രോണർ ഭീമന്റെ കുതികാൽ പിടിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.137; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"घटोत्कचवधपर्व","titleEn":"Ghatotkachavadha Parva (Slaying of Ghatotkacha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"सोमदत्तं तु संप्रेक्ष्य विधुन्वानं महद्धनुः ।\nसात्यकिः प्राह यन्तारं सोमदत्ताय मां वह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Somadatta shaking his great bow, Satyaki said to his charioteer: \"Carry me to Somadatta."}},{"n":2,"text":"न ह्यहत्वा रणे शत्रुं बाह्लीकं कौरवाधमम् ।\nनिवर्तिष्ये रणात्सूत सत्यमेतद्वचो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will not turn back from the battle, charioteer, without killing that enemy, Bahlika (Somadatta), the lowest of the Kauravas. What I say is true.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"ततः संप्रेषयद्यन्ता सैन्धवांस्तान्महाजवान् ।\nतुरङ्गमाञ्शङ्खवर्णान्सर्वशब्दातिगान्रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the charioteer drove on those swift Sindhu horses, conch-white and beyond all sound in battle."}},{"n":4,"text":"तेऽवहन्युयुधानं तु मनोमारुतरंहसः ।\nयथेन्द्रं हरयो राजन्पुरा दैत्यवधोद्यतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They carried Yuyudhana with the speed of mind and wind, O king, as horses once carried Indra when he was set on killing the Daityas."}},{"n":5,"text":"तमापतन्तं संप्रेक्ष्य सात्वतं रभसं रणे ।\nसोमदत्तो महाबाहुरसंभ्रान्तोऽभ्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the eager Satvata coming at him in battle, mighty-armed Somadatta advanced without agitation."}},{"n":6,"text":"विमुञ्चञ्शरवर्षाणि पर्जन्य इव वृष्टिमान् ।\nछादयामास शैनेयं जलदो भास्करं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Releasing showers of arrows like a rain-giving cloud, he covered Shaineya (Satyaki) as a cloud covers the sun."}},{"n":7,"text":"असंभ्रान्तश्च समरे सात्यकिः कुरुपुंगवम् ।\nछादयामास बाणौघैः समन्ताद्भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki, too, unshaken in battle, covered that bull of the Kurus on every side with floods of arrows, best of Bharatas."}},{"n":8,"text":"सोमदत्तस्तु तं षष्ट्या विव्याधोरसि माधवम् ।\nसात्यकिश्चापि तं राजन्नविध्यत्सायकैः शितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Somadatta pierced the Madhava (Satyaki) in the chest with sixty arrows, and Satyaki also, O king, pierced him with sharp shafts."}},{"n":9,"text":"तावन्योन्यं शरैः कृत्तौ व्यराजेतां नरर्षभौ ।\nसुपुष्पौ पुष्पसमये पुष्पिताविव किंशुकौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cut by each other's arrows, those two bulls among men shone like two flowering kimshuka trees in the flower season."}},{"n":10,"text":"रुधिरोक्षितसर्वाङ्गौ कुरुवृष्णियशस्करौ ।\nपरस्परमवेक्षेतां दहन्ताविव लोचनैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their limbs soaked in blood, the glory-makers of the Kurus and the Vrishnis, looked at each other as if burning each other with their eyes."}},{"n":11,"text":"रथमण्डलमार्गेषु चरन्तावरिमर्दनौ ।\nघोररूपौ हि तावास्तां वृष्टिमन्ताविवाम्बुदौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Moving along the circling tracks of their chariots, those two crushers of foes looked terrible, like two rain clouds."}},{"n":12,"text":"शरसंभिन्नगात्रौ तौ सर्वतः शकलीकृतौ ।\nश्वाविधाविव राजेन्द्र व्यदृश्येतां शरक्षतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"With bodies pierced and torn on every side by arrows, they looked, O king of kings, like two porcupines struck by arrows."}},{"n":13,"text":"सुवर्णपुङ्खैरिषुभिराचितौ तौ व्यरोचताम् ।\nखद्योतैरावृतौ राजन्प्रावृषीव वनस्पती ॥","meaning":{"en":"Studded with gold-feathered arrows, they shone like two trees in the rains covered with fireflies, O king."}},{"n":14,"text":"संप्रदीपितसर्वाङ्गौ सायकैस्तौ महारथौ ।\nअदृश्येतां रणे क्रुद्धावुल्काभिरिव कुञ्जरौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their whole bodies set ablaze by arrows, the two great warriors, angry in battle, looked like two elephants struck with firebrands."}},{"n":15,"text":"ततो युधि महाराज सोमदत्तो महारथः ।\nअर्धचन्द्रेण चिच्छेद माधवस्य महद्धनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, great king, the great warrior Somadatta cut the Madhava's great bow in battle with a crescent-headed arrow."}},{"n":16,"text":"अथैनं पञ्चविंशत्या सायकानां समार्पयत् ।\nत्वरमाणस्त्वराकाले पुनश्च दशभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, hurrying in the hour for haste, he struck him with twenty-five arrows, and again with ten."}},{"n":17,"text":"अथान्यद्धनुरादाय सात्यकिर्वेगवत्तरम् ।\nपञ्चभिः सायकैस्तूर्णं सोमदत्तमविध्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Satyaki took another bow, swifter yet, and quickly pierced Somadatta with five arrows."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततोऽपरेण भल्लेन ध्वजं चिच्छेद काञ्चनम् ।\nबाह्लीकस्य रणे राजन्सात्यकिः प्रहसन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, with another broad-headed arrow, Satyaki, as if laughing, cut down the golden banner of Bahlika (Somadatta) in battle, O king."}},{"n":19,"text":"सोमदत्तस्त्वसंभ्रान्तो दृष्ट्वा केतुं निपातितम् ।\nशैनेयं पञ्चविंशत्या सायकानां समाचिनोत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his banner felled, Somadatta, unshaken, loaded Shaineya with twenty-five arrows."}},{"n":20,"text":"सात्वतोऽपि रणे क्रुद्धः सोमदत्तस्य धन्विनः ।\nधनुश्चिच्छेद समरे क्षुरप्रेण शितेन ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Satvata in turn, angry in battle, cut the archer Somadatta's bow with a sharp razor-headed arrow."}},{"n":21,"text":"अथैनं रुक्मपुङ्खानां शतेन नतपर्वणाम् ।\nआचिनोद्बहुधा राजन्भग्नदंष्ट्रमिव द्विपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he heaped on him a hundred bent-jointed, gold-feathered arrows, many times, O king, like a tusker with broken tusks."}},{"n":22,"text":"अथान्यद्धनुरादाय सोमदत्तो महारथः ।\nसात्यकिं छादयामास शरवृष्ट्या महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, taking up another bow, the powerful great warrior Somadatta covered Satyaki with a rain of arrows."}},{"n":23,"text":"सोमदत्तं तु संक्रुद्धो रणे विव्याध सात्यकिः ।\nसात्यकिं चेषुजालेन सोमदत्तो अपीडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki, enraged, pierced Somadatta in battle, and Somadatta in turn pained Satyaki with a net of arrows."}},{"n":24,"text":"दशभिः सात्वतस्यार्थे भीमोऽहन्बाह्लिकात्मजम् ।\nसोमदत्तोऽप्यसंभ्रान्तः शैनेयमवधीच्छरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the Satvata's sake, Bhima struck Bahlika's son with ten arrows; and Somadatta, unshaken, struck Shaineya with arrows too."}},{"n":25,"text":"ततस्तु सात्वतस्यार्थे भैमसेनिर्नवं दृढम् ।\nमुमोच परिघं घोरं सोमदत्तस्य वक्षसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, on behalf of the Satvata, Bhima's son (Ghatotkacha) hurled a new, strong and dreadful iron club at Somadatta's chest."}},{"n":26,"text":"तमापतन्तं वेगेन परिघं घोरदर्शनम् ।\nद्विधा चिच्छेद समरे प्रहसन्निव कौरवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that frightful club came at him with speed, the Kaurava cut it in two in battle, almost laughing."}},{"n":27,"text":"स पपात द्विधा छिन्न आयसः परिघो महान् ।\nमहीधरस्येव महच्छिखरं वज्रदारितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great iron club, cut in two, fell like a great peak of a mountain split by the thunderbolt."}},{"n":28,"text":"ततस्तु सात्यकी राजन्सोमदत्तस्य संयुगे ।\nधनुश्चिच्छेद भल्लेन हस्तावापं च पञ्चभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, in the battle Satyaki cut Somadatta's bow with a broad-headed arrow, and the bow-hand guard with five."}},{"n":29,"text":"चतुर्भिस्तु शरैस्तूर्णं चतुरस्तुरगोत्तमान् ।\nसमीपं प्रेषयामास प्रेतराजस्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"And with four arrows he quickly sent the four excellent horses to the king of the dead, Bharata."}},{"n":30,"text":"सारथेश्च शिरः कायाद्भल्लेन नतपर्वणा ।\nजहार रथशार्दूलः प्रहसञ्शिनिपुंगवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The tiger among charioteers, bull of the Shini line, smiling, took off the charioteer's head from his body with a bent-jointed broad-headed arrow."}},{"n":31,"text":"ततः शरं महाघोरं ज्वलन्तमिव पावकम् ।\nमुमोच सात्वतो राजन्स्वर्णपुङ्खं शिलाशितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Satvata, O king, let fly a most dreadful gold-feathered arrow, sharpened on stone, blazing like fire."}},{"n":32,"text":"स विमुक्तो बलवता शैनेयेन शरोत्तमः ।\nघोरस्तस्योरसि विभो निपपाताशु भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"That best of arrows, shot by mighty Shaineya, fell swiftly, terrible, on his chest, lord, O Bharata."}},{"n":33,"text":"सोऽतिविद्धो बलवता सात्वतेन महारथः ।\nसोमदत्तो महाबाहुर्निपपात ममार च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck deeply by the mighty Satvata, the great warrior, mighty-armed Somadatta, fell and died."}},{"n":34,"text":"तं दृष्ट्वा निहतं तत्र सोमदत्तं महारथाः ।\nमहता शरवर्षेण युयुधानमुपाद्रवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Somadatta slain, the great warriors rushed at Yuyudhana with a heavy rain of arrows."}},{"n":35,"text":"छाद्यमानं शरैर्दृष्ट्वा युयुधानं युधिष्ठिरः ।\nमहत्या सेनया सार्धं द्रोणानीकमुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Yuyudhana covered with arrows, Yudhishthira with a great army rushed at Drona's division."}},{"n":36,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरः क्रुद्धस्तावकानां महाबलम् ।\nशरैर्विद्रावयामास भारद्वाजस्य पश्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, in anger, Yudhishthira drove your mighty force away with arrows, while Drona looked on."}},{"n":37,"text":"सैन्यानि द्रावयन्तं तु द्रोणो दृष्ट्वा युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nअभिदुद्राव वेगेन क्रोधसंरक्तलोचनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Yudhishthira rout the troops, Drona, eyes red with rage, rushed at him with speed."}},{"n":38,"text":"ततः सुनिशितैर्बाणैः पार्थं विव्याध सप्तभिः ।\nसोऽतिविद्धो महाबाहुः सृक्किणी परिसंलिहन् ।\nयुधिष्ठिरस्य चिच्छेद ध्वजं कार्मुकमेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he pierced Partha (Yudhishthira) with seven well-sharpened arrows. Though badly struck, the mighty-armed one, licking the corners of his mouth, cut down Drona's banner and his bow."}},{"n":39,"text":"स छिन्नधन्वा त्वरितस्त्वराकाले नृपोत्तमः ।\nअन्यदादत्त वेगेन कार्मुकं समरे दृढम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With his bow cut, the best of kings quickly, in the hour for haste, took up another strong bow in the battle."}},{"n":40,"text":"ततः शरसहस्रेण द्रोणं विव्याध पार्थिवः ।\nसाश्वसूतध्वजरथं तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the king pierced Drona with a thousand arrows, along with his horses, charioteer, banner and chariot; it was like a marvel."}},{"n":41,"text":"ततो मुहूर्तं व्यथितः शरघातप्रपीडितः ।\nनिषसाद रथोपस्थे द्रोणो भरतसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then for a moment, pained and weakened by the blows of arrows, Drona sank down on the seat of his chariot, best of Bharatas."}},{"n":42,"text":"प्रतिलभ्य ततः संज्ञां मुहूर्ताद्द्विजसत्तमः ।\nक्रोधेन महताविष्टो वायव्यास्त्रमवासृजत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Regaining his senses after a moment, the best of brahmins, filled with great anger, let loose the Vayavya weapon."}},{"n":43,"text":"असंभ्रान्तस्ततः पार्थो धनुराकृष्य वीर्यवान् ।\nतदस्त्रमस्त्रेण रणे स्तम्भयामास भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Partha, powerful and unshaken, drew his bow and stopped that weapon with a weapon in the battle, Bharata."}},{"n":44,"text":"ततोऽब्रवीद्वासुदेवः कुन्तीपुत्रं युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nयुधिष्ठिर महाबाहो यत्त्वा वक्ष्यामि तच्छृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Vasudeva spoke to Kunti's son Yudhishthira: \"Mighty-armed Yudhishthira, listen to what I say."}},{"n":45,"text":"उपारमस्व युद्धाय द्रोणाद्भरतसत्तम ।\nगृध्यते हि सदा द्रोणो ग्रहणे तव संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Stop fighting Drona, best of Bharatas. Drona is always eager to capture you in battle."}},{"n":46,"text":"नानुरूपमहं मन्ये युद्धमस्य त्वया सह ।\nयोऽस्य सृष्टो विनाशाय स एनं श्वो हनिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not think a fight with you suits him. The one who was created for his destruction will kill him tomorrow."}},{"n":47,"text":"परिवर्ज्य गुरुं याहि यत्र राजा सुयोधनः ।\nभीमश्च रथशार्दूलो युध्यते कौरवैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Avoid the teacher and go where King Suyodhana is, where Bhima, tiger among warriors, is fighting with the Kauravas.\""}},{"n":48,"text":"वासुदेववचः श्रुत्वा धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nमुहूर्तं चिन्तयित्वा तु ततो दारुणमाहवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Vasudeva's words, Yudhishthira, king of dharma, thought for a moment, then, into that dreadful battle,"}},{"n":49,"text":"प्रायाद्द्रुतममित्रघ्नो यत्र भीमो व्यवस्थितः ।\nविनिघ्नंस्तावकान्योधान्व्यादितास्य इवान्तकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the slayer of foes quickly went to where Bhima stood, striking your warriors like Death with open mouth."}},{"n":50,"text":"रथघोषेण महता नादयन्वसुधातलम् ।\nपर्जन्य इव घर्मान्ते नादयन्वै दिशो दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the great roar of his chariot he made the earth resound, and sounded all ten directions like a cloud at the end of summer."}},{"n":51,"text":"भीमस्य निघ्नतः शत्रून्पार्ष्णिं जग्राह पाण्डवः ।\nद्रोणोऽपि पाण्डुपाञ्चालान्व्यधमद्रजनीमुखे ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Bhima was killing enemies, the Pandava (Yudhishthira) took the rear guard at his back; and Drona, at the start of night, scattered the Pandavas and Panchalas."}}]}]}